{title: 516 - All the Way}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]All the way [D]my savior [G/D]leads me;
[F#dim]What have I to ask beside?
[G]Can I [C/G]doubt [G]His tender [F#dim]mercy,
[Am/E]Who thro’ life has been my [D/A]guide?
[D/F#]Heav’nly [G]peace divinest comfort,
[G]Here by faith in Him to [F#dim]dwell!
[G]For I know whate’er [C]befall [G]me,
[G/D]Jesus [D]doeth all [G/D]things well;
[G]For I [Bm]know whate’er [C]befall [G]me,
[G/D]Jesus [D7/C]doeth all [Em/B]things well;

Verse 2:
[G]All the way [D]my Savior [G/D]leads me;
[F#dim]Cheers each winding path I [G]tread;
[G]Gives [C/G]me [G]grace for every [F#dim]trial,
[Am/E]Feeds me with the living [D/A]bread;
[D/F#]Though my [G]weary steps may falter,
[G]And my soul athirst may [F#dim]be,
[G]Gushing from the Rock [C]before [G]me,
[G/D]Lo, a spring [D]of joy [G/D]I see;
[G]Gushing [Bm]from the [D7/C]Rock [C]before [G]me,
[G/D]Lo, a spring [D7/C]of joy [Em/B]I see.

Verse 3:
[G]All the way [D]my Savior [G/D]leads me;
[F#dim]O the fullness of His [G]love!
[G]Perfect [C/G]rest [G]to me is [F#dim]promised
[Am/E]In my Father's house above;
[D/F#]When I [G]wake to life immortal,
[G]Wing my flight to realms of [F#dim]day,
[G]This my song through endless [C/G]ages,
[G/D]Jesus led [D]me all [G/D]the way;
[G]This my [Bm]song through [D7/C]endless [C/G]ages,
[G/D]Jesus led [D7/C]me all [Em/B]the way.
